    "guia.g1": "Learning outcomes: the syllabus states only two objectives with non-observable verbs (“Conocer el Cibercrimen como fenómeno”, “Estudiar la Ciberseguridad”), not linked to units or assessment instruments. This app proposes one measurable outcome per unit; it should be validated and, if accepted, added to the syllabus.",
    "guia.g2": "Test formula: the penalty is incorrect / no. of options. The classic correction for guessing uses no. of options − 1; with the current formula, random guessing has a positive expected value (with 4 options, +0.0625 per question). It is worth deciding whether that is intended and publishing the number of options per question, which is not stated.",
    "guia.g3": "Continuous assessment: it is not stated how students who score under 5 in the test after submitting the case are graded, nor what the resit or extraordinary sitting for the case study is.",
    "guia.g4": "Case study: the marking criteria have no weights or performance levels and the “stipulated elements” are not listed. A public rubric with descriptors would improve transparency and feedback before grading.",
    "guia.g5": "Bibliography: the core reference gives no publisher or year; the complementary works date from 2015 and 2017. Cybersecurity regulation in unit 9 has changed since then (e.g. Directive (EU) 2022/2555, NIS2): an up-to-date source should be added.",
    "guia.g6": "Workload and methods: the syllabus lists five teaching methods and 4.5 ECTS (about 112-135 hours of work), but does not split classroom and independent hours or provide assessable test practice before the exam. This app's practice bank is a proposal to fill that gap.",
